@startuml
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
title Recursive decomposition - chunk lifecycle and depth decision (ADR-006)

start
:Lead creates the task card;
:Role d1 reads card inputs (grep/offset, not the corpus);
if (Stage fits one budget unit?) then (yes)
  :Write the artifact in one session;
else (no)
  :Write the chunk plan to docs/chunks/T-XXX.json;
  :chunk-validate.py (schema, owns, coverage);
  repeat
    :Take the next pending chunk;
    :chunk.ps1 claim (state = in_progress);
    if (Chunk fits the budget?) then (yes)
      :Execute at the current depth;
    else (no)
      if (depth < 3) then (yes)
        :Brief, then spawn one same-role child (depth + 1);
        :Child returns paths and <=10 lines;
      else (no, d3)
        :Stop and broaden ownership or split the artifact;
      endif
    endif
    if (Chunk done?) then (yes)
      :chunk.ps1 complete (state = done, produced sha256);
    else (no)
      :chunk.ps1 fail or blocked (attempts + 1);
    endif
  repeat while (Chunks remain?)
endif
:stage-done.ps1 -Chunk / checkpoint gate;
:All chunks done -> checkpoint may close;
stop

note right
  Invariants
  - one child at a time, never parallel
  - same role only (except ux-designer -> coder)
  - a stop is safe only at a chunk boundary
  - depth 4 is never spawned
end note
@enduml
